WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.860
How are the two omelette wraps?

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.980
This one's with chili sauce,

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.230
and this one's with basil sauce.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.240
I can make them better.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:12.860
Huh?!

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.110
Do you guys ever stop eating?

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.200
So, Shiomi-senpai...

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.620
this Stagiaire thing?

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.410
What is that about?

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:25.040
"Stagiaire" is a French 
word meaning "intern."

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:30.670
It's a program to send high school first-years to various businesses in the food industry.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:35.130
They can be high-end restaurants, 
food manufacturers, or even public organizations.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.680
They cover a wide range.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.930
It's an official part of the curriculum 
to give students practical experience.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:42.430
Sounds like a breeze.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:47.400
I doubt even professionals 
would be better than me.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.360
It's not something to take lightly!

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.530
All the Stagiaire partners

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:55.200
have agreed to take on students because they trust the academy.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.240
If you cause any problems that would 
negatively impact Tohtsuki's reputation,

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:01.200
you might even get expelled.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.080
<i>That's right.</i>

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.960
<i>This is the kind of school I'm in.</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.960
<i>So I can go out to work 
in a different kitchen,</i>

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.670
<i>out in the world, 
away from this place!</i>

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:15.130
So you pass if you do your job
 without causing problems?

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:21.140
The criterion for passing is to make a
 "visible mark" during your internship.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.310
A visible... mark?

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.560
{=10}A Few Days Later

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.560
{=10}A Few Days Later

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:33.400
Hm, so the first training 
site is tackled in pairs.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.780
{=0=83}TRAINING PROGRAM GUIDE

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.780
{=0=82}yukihira souma-sama

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:34.900
{=0=83}TRAINING PROGRAM GUIDE

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:42.160
Yukihira... Souma...

00:01:43.080 --> 00:03:10.960
{OP}

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:05.600
Far beyond the image I have in my mind

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:12.070
The reality I'm building up is still far away

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:15.820
An endless journey

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:20.830
Let's hone each other's pride

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.330
Words aren't really important

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.830
So let's just say "yes" and leave it at that

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:32.800
We fight each other and hone our skills

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.680
Our encounters cause shockwaves

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.430
We're reckless challengers

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:45.430
Heading toward a world as yet unexplored

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.980
A swordsman should use his blade

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.810
To open the way to the future

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:56.530
This is my story and no one else's

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.290
Well, let's give it our best, 
Miss Secretary!

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.420
Don't call me that!

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.590
I have no intention of working with you.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:23.340
I'll get through the Stagiaire 
 by my own efforts alone!

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.260
Oh, yeah?

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:28.220
Hm, I wonder what kind 
of restaurant we'll be sent to!

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.350
Don't talk to me!

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.810
Since the almighty Tohtsuki is sending us there,

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.770
I bet it's some ritzy place.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.820
Are you even listening to me?!

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:36.900
This?

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:42.820
How long you gonna make us wait?!

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:43.820
I can't eat in five minutes!

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:44.570
Cancel my order!

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:45.280
I've had enough.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:45.780
Jeez.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:46.410
This is a joke!

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.910
I'm sorry, sorry, so sorry!

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.670
Are you two Tohtsuki students, by any chance?!

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.960
I wish you hadn't seen 
that embarrassing scene just now.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.550
I'm Mitamura, the third 
owner of this restaurant.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.470
Nice to meet you!

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:08.350
I am Arato Hisako. 
I will be here for a week for the Stagiaire.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.680
I am sure I have much to learn,

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.810
so I appreciate you having me here.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.650
I'm Yukihira Souma.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:15.520
Thanks for having me.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.270
I see.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:20.490
Arato-san and Yukihira-kun, huh?

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.360
Well, sorry to cut to the point,

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.820
but can I have your autographs?

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.450
Huh?

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:29.870
I mean, you're students of <i>the</i> 
Tohtsuki Academy, aren't you?!

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:34.170
You might become world-renowned all-star chefs in the future!

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.920
He reminds me of someone.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.210
Souma-chan!

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:43.170
I'm not a chef to be proud of.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.140
Arato, how much longer 
are you gonna take?

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.180
Don't talk to me when I'm still changing!

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.020
Where are your manners?!

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:56.150
Still, it feels new to stand in the kitchen without wearing my Yukihira T-shirt.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:00.440
Sorry to make you wait.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:03.440
You look pretty good in an apron, Arato.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.150
What?!

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:08.370
Come to think of it, this is the first time I've talked to you alone.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.700
You were always with Nakiri.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:12.580
Oh, right!

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:13.960
The next time you see Nakiri—

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:14.960
I...

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.670
I cannot go back to Erina-sama anymore.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:23.210
I have no right, after being 
defeated in the Autumn Selection.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.050
Oh, right.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.840
You lost to Hayama, yeah.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.010
Shut up! Don't laugh!

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:32.010
Erina-sama is invincible and undefeated.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:34.980
If a loser like me stays by her side,

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.980
it'll demean her.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.440
Hurry up.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:46.650
It's quiet.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.860
I can't believe there was 
a commotion here earlier.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.070
All right!

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.870
Let's give it all we've got!

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.540
Oh, so first off, Arato, you can—

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.870
Don't give me orders!

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.370
Listen!

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.710
Don't act superior just because you have practical experience!{try shorten if possible}

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:02.170
I've taken classes where 
I had to cook in teams too.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:05.670
I had no problem finishing tasks 
that required speed during camp.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.760
I'm not going to have any 
problems in the Stagiaire.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.430
But what you said...

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.430
None of those situations involved handling an endless stream of orders, did they?

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:15.680
What?

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:20.900
H...

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:21.520
H...

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.150
Here they come!

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:25.070
<i>Wh-What?!</i>

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.030
<i>Completely full in the blink of an eye?!</i>

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:28.400
Please wait a moment.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:28.400
Are you ready to order?

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:29.780
<i>A barrage of orders?!</i>

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.740
Three Special Lunch Sets, please!

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.740
One Omelette A Set and another D Set.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.830
<i>I had no idea it'd be this bad.</i>

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:37.500
Before, most of our customers used to be locals.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:41.710
Then our nearby train station
 became a bullet train stop.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:44.300
All the people taking 
the bullet train now rush here,

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:47.510
place their orders, and ask to settle the check immediately, so...

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:50.260
<i>So that's why they can't handle this.</i>

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.890
Hey, where's my order?

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.510
I need it soon.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.770
Where are the A and D Sets?!

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.680
Hang on. It'll be five more minutes.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.390
We need to wash dishes!

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.810
We don't have time right now.

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.020
We don't have enough clean dishes!

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.610
I'll do it!

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:07.070
Oh, c'mon!

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.780
I'll have to run to catch my train!

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.360
Please come again!

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:17.240
Again!

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.950
Here they come!

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.710
<i>The next wave, right as I thought we finally had things handled!</i>

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:23.710
<i>This is like a battlefield!</i>

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.420
<i>There isn't a moment's rest between waves!</i>

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.050
Here are some orders!

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:34.550
Table 1 wants a special sandwich,
 two French toasts, and three coffees.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:35.850
The coffee should be after their meal!

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:40.310
Table 3 wants two beef stews, two Napolitans,
 one coffee, two iced coffees, and one melon soda.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:41.810
The Napolitans should have no green peppers!

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:44.190
The food's kind of slow.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.310
I'm not going to make the train.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:47.610
Arato, can you handle the customers?

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:48.280
Huh?

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.700
Table 4's order is up, 
including the Napolitan!

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:54.780
Wow.

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:56.280
Hey!

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.540
I ordered a cheeseburger with cheddar!

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.700
I'm so sorry.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:00.330
We'll make the right o—

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:00.960
Forget it!

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:02.210
I'd be late!

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:02.160
Arato!

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.080
There's bad communication between the kitchen and the servers.{needs to be shorter}

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:05.750
Can you go check it out?

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:08.340
<i>No way. Giving me orders?{timing split here is f**ked}</i>

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.920
<i>Who does he think he is?!</i>

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:18.140
<i>Everything about you is too small.</i>

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:19.600
<i>But what you said...</i>

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:23.480
<i>None of those situations involved handling an endless stream of orders, did they?</i>

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:27.980
<i>I can't show my face to Erina-sama.</i>

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:33.860
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:38.660
Thank you so much!

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:41.040
It's over!

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.410
We made it through!

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:44.000
That was wonderful!

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.040
Without you, 
we wouldn't have made it!

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:48.790
Yeah, it was amazing!

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:51.670
Tohtsuki's students sure are different.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:55.220
Yes. He has practical experience, as well.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:57.300
What? We're talking about you too.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.810
By dinnertime, 
you were up to speed.

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.680
You're a quick learner and flexible too.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.640
You were a huge help.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.480
Thank you.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:12.320
What was that for?! How rude!

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:13.990
Good work!

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:16.820
Keep up the good work 
tomorrow too, Arato!

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.120
Don't give me orders!

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:23.250
Yeah, yeah. Got it.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:26.920
I refuse.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:29.170
What did you say?

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:33.380
I am saying that I won't wash dishes 
or anything of that sort.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.470
I believe delegating trivial tasks to me

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:38.970
is nothing other than 
a foolish error in judgment.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:43.470
You're just a student. 
Get over yourself.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:48.150
<i>Souma-kun! Things are looking 
pretty rocky on my end!</i>

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.940
Man, you were a huge help today too.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:54.740
It was a great idea to accept interns.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.370
Is that a photo of this restaurant?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.530
Yeah.

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.790
It's from back when my dad used to be the chef.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:08.420
I still remember how all 
the local regulars worshipped him.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:12.840
Your restaurant does have a wide selection,

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.130
and you season your dishes {very }carefully.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:15.130
Yeah.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:16.920
That's about the only thing I'm proud of.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:20.470
I want to try hard and work toward that ideal restaurant from the past.

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:30.440
What're you slacking for, 
Yukihira Souma?

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.900
We're not done cleaning yet!

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.230
Is this good enough?

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.860
Leaving a visible mark...

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.070
Is this what it means?

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:41.820
What are you talking about?

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:44.200
The program's going quite well.

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.290
Well, I guess.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.670
By the way, I wonder how the others are doing?

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.330
I wonder what kind of restaurants they ended up in?

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.340
<i>I'm sure Erina-sama is doing well,</i>

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:58.970
<i>even without me.</i>

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:00.300
Wonderful, Chef!

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:03.390
The dishes have been refined above and beyond what they used to be!

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:07.100
The redesigned course menu
 is novel and bold too! Perfect!

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.060
With this, you'll get 
a Michelin star next year for sure!

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:12.690
Th-Thank you. It's an honor.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:17.530
Erina-sama, please check the taste!

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:19.450
Erina-sama, sorry to keep 
you waiting on the prep work!

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:23.070
Saucier, you are 50 seconds behind schedule.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:23.700
Sorry!

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.160
Good.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:26.790
Please serve it to the customers.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:27.370
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:31.170
<i>My castle... was taken over... 
by that little bitch</i>

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:34.250
<i>before I even knew it.</i>

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:36.090
Chef Kasayama.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:38.210
About the main dish...

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:44.180
I believe the texture can be improved if it is poached at a slightly lower temperature.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:47.430
There are about twelve other issues I'd like to discuss with you.

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:50.390
Would that be all right?

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:56.770
Please do.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.280
Then first, regarding the hors d'oeuvre...

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:03.320
<i>There has to be something I can do too.</i>

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.740
Man, this just isn't cutting it.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.540
That again?

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:11.580
What do you find lacking?

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:16.540
They make solid food, their staff are all nice, 
and they care about their restaurant.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:20.300
I want to help them as much as I can.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:21.670
Hey...

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:23.380
Is this good enough for you?

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:24.130
Huh?

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:27.350
That restaurant isn't where
 you really want to be, right?

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:30.720
I think that the restaurant has to change.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:32.310
Besides...

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:33.770
Well, never mind.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:36.150
Anyway, see you tomorrow!

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.320
Good morning, Arato-san.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:45.820
Please take care of the delivery slips today.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:47.910
Yes, sir. I'm already on it.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.490
Okay, thank you!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.000
<i>This restaurant has to change?</i>

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.840
<i>What do you mean by that, 
Yukihira Souma?</i>

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:01.300
<i>That restaurant isn't where
 you really want to be, right?</i>

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.550
Remember who he is.

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:06.930
See?

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:10.010
Ever since we came, sales have gone up, and complaints have gone down.

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:15.140
When... we leave...

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:15.560
Right.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.770
They'll be right back where they started.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:25.610
Of course, adding more bodies during crunch 
time will help keep the restaurant running,

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.740
but it doesn't really solve the root problem.

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.240
Should we let things stay the way they are?

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.410
We're holding an emergency meeting!

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:42.710
<i>If I don't do something, the Stagiaire will end 
with me only having done trivial tasks.</i>

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:46.300
<i>I can't do anything amazing like Nakiri-san,</i>

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:49.390
<i>but I have to be more useful!</i>

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:50.760
Here's the next batch!

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.060
Oh, okay!

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:00.860
Let's advertise a part-time job right now!

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:05.030
We have to find new help before the Tohtsuki students leave!

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:09.570
But do you think we can easily find people who can fill their shoes?

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:13.290
Should we cut down the menu?

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:18.080
The large menu has become a liability.

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:20.500
If you print a new menu, keeping only the customers' favorites—

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.840
No!

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.340
There are recipes in there 
from my grandfather's day!

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.630
If you keep on the way you have, 
this restaurant will eventually go under—

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:31.050
Hey, we're grateful for your help and all.

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.720
But making such a huge change...

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:37.060
We've been working here 
since the previous owner's time.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:40.440
If we change the menu,
 it wouldn't be Mitamura anymore.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:44.570
But don't you feel sorry for the customers?

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:46.820
Even though they chose this place to come into,

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.740
they can't get the food they ordered. It's not even about the taste.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:50.990
That's unacceptable!

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:53.830
Mitamura-san.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.830
What kind of restaurant
 do you want this place to be?

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:01.290
There's something I want you to consider.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:03.790
Excuse me.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:04.840
Hello?

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:05.460
What?

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:09.930
About the second course, the fish salad...

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:11.680
What, you too?!

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.390
Go back to washing dishes!

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:15.890
Okay, sorry!

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:17.020
It's fine.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:18.020
Tell us.

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:20.520
Um...

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:26.110
I thought it'd be nice if customers could choose how much sauce they want to pour on.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:30.320
The dishes that come in either tend to have a lot of leftover sauce,

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:33.490
or, if customers used bread 
to soak up the sauce,

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.780
a lot of leftover vegetables.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:40.500
<i>She found something to improve,
 just from washing dishes?</i>

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.880
But it might be difficult to do.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:45.920
It'll mean more work for the hall and kitchen staff.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:46.630
No.

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:50.380
Serving the sauce in a saucière

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:53.340
has been a widespread practice
 in France for a long time.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:57.140
Reverting to such a tradition
 may actually be quite novel.

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:59.100
Cut it out already!

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:01.810
The customers are coming 
here to eat <i>my</i> food!

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.270
Who cares about the amount of sauce—

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:04.440
Um, Chef!

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:05.190
What?!

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:08.480
A customer's requesting more sauce.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.410
Thank you! Please come again!

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.040
Going to reservations only?!

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:27.670
Mitamura's food is good.
 There's no questioning that.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:31.970
Thanks to your careful work and the large menu, customers are always satisfied.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:35.800
But those virtues have faded

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:37.970
because of the changes in the area.

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:40.850
So I think this is a possible 
option for you to take.

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.560
It's too bad for customers 
trying to drop in, but...

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.940
Reservations only, huh?

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:49.980
It's easy to say, 
but will it actually work?

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:53.530
It's a huge risk to turn away customers who find their way to our door.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:58.080
Why do we now suddenly have to change how we've been doing things?

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.660
If the circumstances have changed,

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:04.120
and you don't also change,
 you won't be able to move forward!

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:07.460
If there is something 
you really want to pursue,

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:09.630
you should cling to it without
 worrying about appearances!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:13.010
I believe this restaurant has great potential.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.630
I want to believe that.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:21.470
Well, we won't be the ones 
who make that decision.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:24.560
It's the man at the top, 
right? Mitamura-san?

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.860
What is it you want to pursue as the chef?

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:31.360
Welcome!

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:34.360
Shimizu-san, thank you 
for the reservation!

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.860
Hey, sorry for not coming by for a while.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.740
It seemed really busy recently,

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:42.080
so I found it hard to drop in.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:44.710
Now that you're only allowing reservations,
 I came rushing back!

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:48.330
I want the usual Napolitan 
and two side dishes.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:49.460
Oh, and...

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:51.090
Cut back a bit on the salt, right?

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.420
You know me, 
third-generation chef!

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.180
Thank you for waiting.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:05.680
Oh, yes.

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.310
The food here tastes just 
as good as I remember.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:10.020
May I have coffee afterward, as well?

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:11.900
Of course.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:19.110
<i>It seems they've overcome one of the criteria for passing the Stagiaire.</i>

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:22.910
<i>It's not just enough 
to handle the job you were given.</i>

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:26.500
<i>You have to figure out what you can do to improve the restaurant and take action.</i>

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:29.460
<i>That's the first step in the Stagiaire.</i>

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:33.670
You were looking pretty blue on the first day,
 but you look like you're feeling a bit better now.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:34.920
Hmph.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.050
If you have time to waste in idle talk,

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:39.260
you can work harder, Yukihira Souma!

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:42.850
Glad you liked it!

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:46.220
It's, "Thank you! Please come again!"

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:47.730
Don't start using your own catchphrase!

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:53.320
You've passed the first Stagiaire.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:54.320
Huh?

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.940
Your work was faultless, both of you.

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:58.110
Thank you.

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:00.160
Where were they watching us from?

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:01.700
Tohtsuki sure is amazing.

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:05.450
Information about the next training location should be delivered by tomorrow.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.450
Good luck.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:12.330
By the way, Arato.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:14.290
You're going to go back to 
Nakiri's place soon, aren't you?

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:17.460
Not again.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:19.090
What's wrong? Cheer up.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:21.010
I'll hear you out.

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:28.430
<i>I-I'm so nervous!{she's using her local dialect, but I'm not gonna try an English equivalent}</i>

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:30.480
<i>Why is this happening?!</i>

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:33.060
<i>You seem to have a lot of luggage.</i>

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:34.650
<i>I'll give you a ride.</i>

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:40.530
I don't know why someone with your talent has been unknown for so long.

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:42.990
<i>Wh-What? 
This is embarrassing.</i>

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:48.410
What was the score on your high school division entrance exam?

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:50.870
Um, it was really low!

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:53.630
<i>I can't tell her I got the worst grade!</i>

00:19:54.330 --> 00:20:00.050
But I didn't make my way back
 from that all by myself.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:03.890
I managed to survive camp and
 enter the Autumn Selection

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:07.350
thanks to everyone 
at the dorm and Souma-kun.

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:09.810
When I first saw Souma-kun,

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:13.270
I made up my mind 
to stay as far away as I could,

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:15.190
but we somehow became friends.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:17.940
Please don't talk any more about him!

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:19.860
Oh, sorry.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:22.610
<i>I wonder if I said something 
that got on her nerves.</i>

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:26.370
By the way, Nakiri-san, 
you're always with Arato-san, right?

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:28.240
What?

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:29.330
Um, is something wrong?!

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.500
<i>Hisako...</i>

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:33.540
<i>See, Hisako?</i>

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:36.540
<i>The cherry blossoms are so pretty!</i>

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.340
<i>You should come over here too!</i>

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:43.010
<i>Oh, that would be improper!</i>

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:45.720
<i>I'll stay behind you, Erina-sama.</i>

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:47.600
<i>I am your aide.</i>

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:51.520
<i>Hisako...</i>

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:55.310
<i>What I wanted back then was for you to...</i>

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:58.900
How pathetic.

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:01.320
I still lack confidence somehow.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.990
I think I've been too complacent.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:07.660
I was fine as long as I could 
walk behind Erina-sama.

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.490
I didn't want anything more.

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:13.620
So why are you stressing out?

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:15.000
Did you even hear what I said?!

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.880
The answer's simple.

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:20.130
From now on, try to become someone

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:24.590
who can walk beside her 
instead of behind her.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:28.300
I lost to Hayama too.

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:31.850
So let's beat him someday, yeah?

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:36.020
But... I lost. I don't have the right...

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:39.110
If there's something you 
really want to pursue,

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:40.770
you cling to it without 
worrying about appearances.

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:42.860
You said that.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:47.240
Oh, and these belong 
to one of my dorm mates,

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:49.570
but she said she could spare them for a bit.

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:53.120
I promised Nakiri she could read them,

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:55.080
but it's hard to find time to drop them off.

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:57.120
So this is a great opportunity.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:59.540
Take them to Nakiri, will you?

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:01.380
Thanks, Arato.

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:03.380
Don't drop them on the way, yeah?

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:08.090
Yukihira Souma...

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:12.060
Thank you.

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:14.850
<i>Come over here.</i>

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:31.410
<i>I'm the same way, Arato.</i>

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:39.040
<i>In the end, my cooking may have just been me chasing after my dad!</i>

00:22:35.150 --> 00:22:37.150
{meme}

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:45.090
<i>I'm gonna take my time and check out the cooking world 
outside of Yukihira, with wide-open eyes!</i>

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:49.550
<i>Then I'm gonna shine a new 
light on my own cooking!</i>

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:51.140
All right!

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:53.310
Where's the next Stagiaire?!

00:22:56.160 --> 00:23:01.040
An intensely burning desire was born

00:23:01.040 --> 00:23:06.880
But not in me, in someone else

00:23:06.880 --> 00:23:11.680
Where's the me who believed that

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:16.810
All one needs is to have hopes and dreams

00:23:16.810 --> 00:23:22.060
Wrapped around something long, my compass was lost

00:23:22.060 --> 00:23:27.820
On the border of life and death, snow drops bloom

00:23:27.820 --> 00:23:33.160
If by some mistake they get smashed

00:23:33.160 --> 00:23:38.330
At least put flowers on the empty husk

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:44.000
Is that the way things are? Yes, it is

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:49.050
You can call it resignation if you want

00:23:49.050 --> 00:23:54.970
But that's not me, that's not me

00:23:54.970 --> 00:23:59.600
There's no value in something just anyone could make

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:10.970
Next time, "The Magician Once More."

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:10.970
THE MAGICIAN RETURNS
